-- Migration: Store LUZZI's formatted text (poetic lines, italics) and title_position
--
-- Requires 019 (text_plain, title_position, bibleget_plain_text()) and 015.
--
-- luzzi.txt (LaParola.net "Luzzi/Riveduta") marks poetic lines with <br />
-- and italics with <i>. They were flattened by the 2015 import; this puts
-- them back into `text`, using the NABRE tag set that the clients already
-- render (WordPress, Google Docs, MediaWiki):
--
--   * Psalms (the only book LaParola lays out line by line): each poetic
--     line is a <po> line, lines joined by "\n"; a poem starts with <pof>
--     (at a chapter start, after a heading, or after a superscription /
--     lead-in) and ends with <pol> (the line with no trailing <br />,
--     including a one-line verse that closes a poem left open by the
--     previous verse, or where the next verse opens a heading or prose).
--     LaParola carries no stanza or indent information, so there is no <poi>.
--   * Every other book is laid out as prose paragraphs: there a trailing
--     <br /> only ends a paragraph and is dropped (no paragraph construct to
--     store it in), and the rare inner <br /> (~40 verses: lead-ins, the end
--     of a quoted song, e.g. Josh 10:13, Lk 1:46) is kept as an untagged line
--     break. No poetry tags are invented where the source marks none.
--   * a psalm superscription or prose lead-in ("…e disse:") stays an
--     untagged line before the poem, as in NABRE;
--   * <i> is kept (Old Testament quotations in the New, superscriptions,
--     Sela), closed and reopened at line ends so every line is well nested.
--
-- title_position is set for the 4 verses whose heading falls mid-verse
-- (2 Kgs 25:21, Neh 7:73, John 12:36, Acts 9:19): the heading goes right
-- after the space that follows the sentence before it.
--
-- Safety: each UPDATE matches the current plain text AND requires
-- bibleget_plain_text(new formatted text) = that plain text, so text_plain
-- and text_hash -- and with them the embeddings -- cannot change. The
-- title_position CHECK constraint validates every offset. Idempotent: once
-- applied, `text` no longer equals the plain text and nothing matches.
--
-- Generated by scripts/repair_luzzi_from_source.py --emit formatted.

BEGIN;

